   "evidence": "The probe uses two real Store connections and interleaves B's initialization after A reads absence. HEAD performs `const existing = store.getSetting<string | null>(\"member.id\", null)`, then `store.setSetting(\"member.id\", id); return id;`. Store.setSetting uses `ON CONFLICT(key) DO UPDATE SET value = excluded.value`, allowing A to overwrite B's winner. Store's upsert existed at base, but memberId and this unsafe initialization are new; claim-ref.ts does not exist at base. The later implementation uses INSERT OR IGNORE and reads back the stored identity; the same probe then reports distinctReturnedIds=false and bIdentityChanged=false."
